WEBVTT

00:56.973 --> 00:59.350
There's this phrase in The Art of War.

01:00.018 --> 01:02.145
"Attack is the secret of defense."

01:02.854 --> 01:05.356
But I'm not sure about that.
I don't exactly agree.

01:06.024 --> 01:09.110
It's hard enough defending yourself.
You won't have the strength to attack.

01:09.194 --> 01:11.946
So I believe the best defense

01:12.864 --> 01:14.115
is running away.

01:14.741 --> 01:15.867
UNG IN ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

01:15.950 --> 01:18.870
I have a long history of running away.

01:18.953 --> 01:22.999
In our next class, we'll make
a presentation about our families.

01:23.875 --> 01:25.001
Choi Ung, you can start.

01:25.085 --> 01:26.711
Ung, are you ready?

01:27.796 --> 01:31.508
Let's begin after a short break.

01:31.591 --> 01:33.468
- Okay!
- Okay!

01:33.551 --> 01:35.345
Hey, look.

01:35.428 --> 01:37.889
Let's play with this!

01:38.515 --> 01:40.683
What should we do today?

01:40.767 --> 01:42.227
- Hey!
- Yes! I won!

01:43.853 --> 01:46.898
Ung, come down. Ung!

01:46.981 --> 01:48.066
Come down!

01:48.149 --> 01:49.400
- It's dangerous.
- Come down.

01:49.484 --> 01:50.944
At quite a young age…

01:51.027 --> 01:52.487
- Ung, come down.
- Come on, Ung.

01:52.570 --> 01:55.323
- You'll get hurt!
- It's dangerous. Come on.

01:55.406 --> 01:56.449
- You could get hurt.
- Come down.

01:56.533 --> 01:58.660
- It's dangerous.
- I won't make you do it.

01:58.743 --> 02:00.787
So come down. I mean it.

02:00.870 --> 02:03.081
I promise. You don't have
to do the presentation.

02:03.164 --> 02:05.959
- …I tasted how sweet it could be.
- Come down, all right?

02:07.836 --> 02:11.548
UNG IN HIGH SCHOOL

02:11.631 --> 02:14.843
Of course, I run away for my sake.

02:14.926 --> 02:15.969
Choi Ung!

02:16.553 --> 02:18.471
That brat completely broke this.

02:19.139 --> 02:21.850
- Stop right there!
- But it's also for the other person.

02:21.933 --> 02:23.434
You jerk!

02:23.518 --> 02:25.979
It's to give them time

02:26.062 --> 02:29.232
when they get too emotional
and lose the ability to think clearly.

02:31.192 --> 02:32.527
This cost 29,900 won!

02:34.654 --> 02:36.865
UNG IN UNIVERSITY

02:36.948 --> 02:38.700
I swear I won't hit you!

02:41.828 --> 02:43.079
And I won't yell at you.

02:43.580 --> 02:44.747
So come here.

02:45.707 --> 02:49.752
I'm buying time for them
so we can have a calm conversation.

02:49.836 --> 02:50.879
Do you mean it?

02:53.965 --> 02:54.966
Come here.

02:59.137 --> 03:00.096
Stop right there!

03:02.015 --> 03:05.393
But that doesn't mean
I always run away from everything.

03:06.060 --> 03:08.813
- You're entering a marathon?
- Yes.

03:09.439 --> 03:12.817
Yeon-su said if I do a half marathon,
she'll wear matching rings.

03:12.901 --> 03:14.068
My gosh.

03:14.861 --> 03:17.155
She really is amazing.

03:17.947 --> 03:19.991
Is she dating or babysitting?

03:20.867 --> 03:22.702
She still doesn't know me well enough.

03:22.785 --> 03:24.203
I'm a man of my word.

03:24.996 --> 03:30.293
Hey, I'm going to be tough with you,
so don't go back on your word.

03:30.376 --> 03:32.086
We'll run for an hour every day.

03:32.170 --> 03:33.421
Of course.

03:33.504 --> 03:37.258
With a week of training, I'll even be
able to complete a full marathon.

03:37.926 --> 03:39.093
I'll get going.

03:41.387 --> 03:42.722
Jeez.

03:51.773 --> 03:53.775
I can't do this anymore.

04:24.430 --> 04:25.765
INCOMING CALL
KIM JI-UNG

04:28.059 --> 04:31.813
I make objective judgments
to make the best decision.

04:31.896 --> 04:33.356
INCOMING CALL
KIM JI-UNG

04:37.777 --> 04:41.823
Right. I can just wear
friendship rings with Ji-ung.

04:41.906 --> 04:43.032
Right.

04:53.334 --> 04:55.545
So I'm not embarrassed about running away.

04:56.212 --> 04:59.674
UNG IN THE PRESENT

05:06.931 --> 05:08.349
Now that we've reunited,

05:10.435 --> 05:12.186
we can say, "Have you been well?"

05:13.021 --> 05:14.605
"How have you been?"

05:16.065 --> 05:17.317
"Was it tough for you?"

05:19.736 --> 05:22.488
"It was tough for me."
Can't we tell each other these things?

05:23.614 --> 05:25.033
Darn it…

05:32.749 --> 05:35.418
I asked you for a writer a long time ago.

05:35.501 --> 05:37.045
You're finally sending me one?

05:37.128 --> 05:39.756
Well, you know…

05:42.425 --> 05:45.428
I did my best to find one for you,
so don't give me a hard time.

05:45.511 --> 05:47.305
Everyone's working on something.

05:47.388 --> 05:49.849
There wasn't anyone to send to you.

05:49.932 --> 05:51.017
So…

05:51.517 --> 05:54.145
Well, good luck.

05:54.729 --> 05:57.565
What? Who is it?
Why are you making such excuses?

06:06.282 --> 06:08.701
What are you waiting for?

06:08.785 --> 06:10.912
Are you going to just stand there all day?

06:11.829 --> 06:14.207
You know you're overqualified
to be working on this.

06:14.290 --> 06:16.292
Why are you here?

06:16.375 --> 06:18.336
This is just a simple project.

06:18.419 --> 06:20.630
I'll just get the rookie writers to help.

06:20.713 --> 06:22.965
Do you think I wanted to do this?

06:23.049 --> 06:26.677
But Mr. Park desperately
asked for my help.

06:26.761 --> 06:28.846
You said you were going to work
on dramas now.

06:28.930 --> 06:31.390
- So just go and write--
- I am.

06:31.474 --> 06:33.810
I hate it when people tell me to write
when I'm already writing.

06:34.894 --> 06:36.521
I came here to clear my head a bit,

06:36.604 --> 06:39.440
so don't stop making it so obvious
that you don't want me here.

06:40.358 --> 06:43.736
- So you'll do whatever you want again?
- Things turn out great that way.

06:43.820 --> 06:45.404
I don't like it when you do that.

06:45.488 --> 06:48.324
- I…
- I saw the preview, and it was awful.

06:50.493 --> 06:51.953
Who said you could show her?

06:52.036 --> 06:55.414
What in the world
are you filming, Mr. Kim?

06:55.498 --> 06:59.001
I don't get what you're trying to say
through these videos.

06:59.085 --> 07:01.212
What has gotten into you?

07:01.295 --> 07:05.174
- Have you lost your touch?
- I'll take care of this myself,

07:05.258 --> 07:07.009
so go back to where you came from

07:07.093 --> 07:09.846
or go and clear your head somewhere else.

07:09.929 --> 07:11.139
Mr. Kim.

07:13.808 --> 07:16.853
We're in a bad situation.
We really do need a writer.

07:17.812 --> 07:20.982
Well, I do have something
I want to make up for too.

07:22.358 --> 07:24.485
I won't be that stubborn this time.

07:36.122 --> 07:37.206
So…

07:39.041 --> 07:40.501
what is it that you want to say?

07:43.087 --> 07:46.424
I heard the cast are your friends.
Is that why you were being lazy?

07:48.009 --> 07:51.804
Honestly, I was thinking of refusing this
when I first saw the videos.

07:53.055 --> 07:56.142
But then I found something interesting.

07:56.809 --> 07:59.562
- So I watched the old documentary.
- And?

07:59.645 --> 08:04.066
There seems to be something
going on between the two of them.

08:07.403 --> 08:10.364
There's no way you didn't notice that.

08:11.949 --> 08:14.994
If we use that, I think we can make
quite an interesting piece.

08:15.495 --> 08:17.955
I don't want to force a scenario on them.

08:18.539 --> 08:20.541
No, it actually felt like

08:20.625 --> 08:24.462
the camera was purposely
trying to ignore that side of them.

08:24.545 --> 08:25.546
But…

08:26.547 --> 08:29.467
- Maybe that was just me.
- Why would I purposely do that?

08:29.550 --> 08:31.594
I was trying to film them objectively--

08:31.677 --> 08:33.679
Then why should people film things?

08:33.763 --> 08:36.182
You can let machines do the shooting then.

08:36.265 --> 08:40.228
My gosh. You really haven't
changed a bit, Mr. Kim.

08:42.104 --> 08:46.484
Well, you made the scenes
look quite pretty.

08:47.401 --> 08:48.861
I'll write up something

08:49.987 --> 08:51.572
based on them.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.249
- Hey, you're up.
- Hey.

09:01.332 --> 09:02.792
Today's the party.

09:02.875 --> 09:04.252
Look behind you.

09:04.877 --> 09:08.965
I put in so much effort to prepare
for your debut anniversary party.

09:10.216 --> 09:13.052
Right. And Yeon-su's coming too
because we're filming.

09:14.720 --> 09:16.722
Is there anyone else we can invite?

09:17.390 --> 09:18.891
Like NJ, you know.

09:18.975 --> 09:20.101
Or NJ.

09:20.184 --> 09:21.394
Or NJ.

09:24.063 --> 09:26.274
Right, and Ji-ung said
he's coming early today.

09:26.983 --> 09:27.817
I'll be needing these.

09:30.152 --> 09:33.489
Ung! Ji-ung said he's coming over first
so get ready, okay?

09:33.573 --> 09:36.158
Running away isn't about avoiding things,

09:37.118 --> 09:38.953
 it's just a reasonable decision.

09:52.425 --> 09:53.551
Running away?

09:56.762 --> 10:01.434
I've never done anything so cowardly
in my entire life.

10:12.987 --> 10:16.365
It's all just a pathetic excuse.

10:24.165 --> 10:25.791
Sorry.

10:26.917 --> 10:28.836
I'm quite drunk right now.

10:38.763 --> 10:42.933
Running away is what cowards do.

10:51.359 --> 10:52.526
So?

10:52.610 --> 10:54.487
Did you all read it?

10:57.198 --> 10:58.574
I guess you didn't.

10:58.658 --> 11:02.745
I'm sure you wouldn't be making
such faces after reading my draft.

11:02.828 --> 11:04.955
Sorry, but we can't film

11:05.873 --> 11:06.832
your amazing story.

11:06.916 --> 11:08.084
What? Why?

11:10.378 --> 11:15.091
Don't you think it's a bit
too childish to reject my work like this?

11:16.092 --> 11:17.802
- They ran away.
- Who?

11:17.885 --> 11:19.970
- The cast.
- The cast?

11:20.054 --> 11:21.263
Choi Ung.

11:22.556 --> 11:24.558
Go get him then. It's no big deal.

11:24.642 --> 11:26.060
And Kook Yeon-su too.

11:31.899 --> 11:34.610
EPISODE 7
CATCH ME IF YOU CAN

11:34.693 --> 11:40.366
CELEBRATION PARTY
CHOI UNG, KOOK YEON-SU

11:41.117 --> 11:44.203
ONE HOUR EARLIER

11:53.671 --> 11:56.424
I told you I tried calling him.
He's not picking up.

11:56.507 --> 11:58.175
But you were with him this morning.

11:58.259 --> 12:01.137
Yes. He was here, but he just disappeared.

12:02.054 --> 12:04.432
Did you really not hear anything
from Yeon-su?

12:04.515 --> 12:05.766
Me?

12:06.684 --> 12:09.687
I'm the one who brought all this wine.

12:09.770 --> 12:13.524
I even closed the bar today
to attend this party.

12:13.607 --> 12:14.942
And now this?

12:15.818 --> 12:17.403
Don't you think I'm a victim too?

12:17.486 --> 12:21.574
I get that Choi Ung could do this,
but Yeon-su isn't this irresponsible.

12:23.492 --> 12:25.870
You don't think something's
happened to them, do you?

12:25.953 --> 12:27.913
Didn't you take her home last night?

12:28.497 --> 12:29.665
Maybe she's hungover.

12:30.541 --> 12:32.126
She rarely is, though.

12:33.085 --> 12:34.670
I'll try calling her grandma.

12:38.591 --> 12:39.884
I see.

12:40.551 --> 12:43.804
- What? Is it Yeon-su?
- So she did go AWOL.

12:44.763 --> 12:48.559
"I need time to think.
Don't tell my grandma."

12:49.935 --> 12:52.188
Judging from her rude text,
she hasn't been kidnapped.

12:52.271 --> 12:54.440
Yeon-su went AWOL?

12:54.523 --> 12:57.151
- Why? Why would she do that?
- Where could Ung be?

12:57.234 --> 12:59.612
You know how simple he is.

12:59.695 --> 13:02.740
If we just look around the neighborhood,
we'll find him right away.

13:03.365 --> 13:05.910
But why is he suddenly acting like this?

13:05.993 --> 13:08.245
The drawing show went well yesterday.

13:08.329 --> 13:09.997
I really don't get it.

13:10.789 --> 13:14.710
But isn't it a bit strange for them
to do this at the same time?

13:14.793 --> 13:17.838
Maybe something happened
between the two of them.

13:19.215 --> 13:20.174
Don't you think so?

13:21.342 --> 13:22.510
Is it just me?

13:22.593 --> 13:25.262
I never saw them together
yesterday though.

13:25.346 --> 13:29.642
Right. And Yeon-su came to my bar
after the event ended,

13:29.725 --> 13:32.061
and she went home drunk.

13:32.144 --> 13:34.563
Ung went to bed early last night too.

13:54.917 --> 13:57.670
Was I drunk last night?

13:59.296 --> 14:00.339
No.

14:00.422 --> 14:03.300
Did I take pills yesterday?

14:06.095 --> 14:07.263
No.

14:07.346 --> 14:11.308
Did I cry in front of Yeon-su regardless?

14:27.032 --> 14:28.033
But…

14:28.951 --> 14:31.954
she might not remember either
since she was drunk.

14:38.043 --> 14:39.628
GU EUN-HO

14:39.712 --> 14:41.839
Where are you? Just tell us where you are.

14:41.922 --> 14:44.300
Is this because I asked for a raise?
I'm not giving up though.

14:44.383 --> 14:46.385
Are you with Yeon-su?

14:46.468 --> 14:48.971
Why did you two suddenly go AWOL?

14:54.143 --> 14:57.187
I'll avoid it for now
and think things through.

15:07.740 --> 15:09.909
I did expect this, but…

15:10.701 --> 15:12.453
I've got nowhere to go.

15:14.079 --> 15:17.666
What do people usually do
when they're in my situation?

15:27.885 --> 15:28.844
Right.

15:31.639 --> 15:33.307
I don't have any friends.

15:39.980 --> 15:42.441
I'm not running away.

15:42.524 --> 15:45.819
I'm just keeping a distance
until I can get my thoughts in order.

15:49.949 --> 15:51.867
This is so intriguing.

15:52.826 --> 15:53.911
Pardon?

15:54.536 --> 15:57.831
So they both ran away? My goodness.

15:59.416 --> 16:03.963
This is even better than I thought!
Isn't it strange that they both went AWOL?

16:04.922 --> 16:06.048
It is.

16:06.131 --> 16:07.049
Right?

16:07.800 --> 16:09.677
This is going to be big.

16:09.760 --> 16:11.303
There must be something going on!

16:11.387 --> 16:14.306
I need to be able to film them first
for a chance at success.

16:14.390 --> 16:16.642
What can I do when the cast is gone?

16:17.184 --> 16:18.978
What has gotten into you?

16:19.061 --> 16:21.772
- You don't seem enthusiastic about this.
- What?

16:21.855 --> 16:24.733
When have you ever given up
just because the cast ran away?

16:24.817 --> 16:26.276
Remember Jukdo?

16:26.360 --> 16:27.653
Why bring that up?

16:27.736 --> 16:31.323
You searched the whole island
when the cast went AWOL.

16:31.407 --> 16:33.283
Plus, that snake farm.

16:33.367 --> 16:36.203
You ran around the mountain
looking for the snake that escaped.

16:36.286 --> 16:38.789
And you're saying you can't film
just because of this?

16:38.872 --> 16:40.082
Even if I do find them,

16:40.165 --> 16:43.752
would I be able to film anything good
by forcing them to stay on camera?

16:43.836 --> 16:45.087
If you bring them back,

16:46.171 --> 16:48.298
make sure they can never run away again.

16:50.300 --> 16:51.552
Let's see…

16:52.886 --> 16:55.014
Do you prefer mountains or islands?

16:55.681 --> 16:56.849
Pardon?

16:58.684 --> 17:00.227
Hey, Intern.

17:00.310 --> 17:02.980
What are my works the most known for?

17:03.063 --> 17:07.192
Bringing out people's primal emotions
in a confined environment.

17:08.110 --> 17:09.069
Say that more simply.

17:10.529 --> 17:12.072
Locking them up and filming?

17:13.115 --> 17:15.451
The weather's nice these days.
Let's go on a trip.

17:16.493 --> 17:18.829
Kidnap the cast,
take them somewhere secluded,

17:18.912 --> 17:20.748
and film them for about three days.

17:24.793 --> 17:26.670
All right, don't worry.

17:26.754 --> 17:28.839
I'm doing my best to find him.

17:28.922 --> 17:31.508
Yes. I'll call you when I find him.

17:31.592 --> 17:34.011
Oh, there's my taxi. Taxi!

17:34.094 --> 17:35.304
I'll call you later.

17:41.810 --> 17:43.103
Thank you, Choi Ung.

17:44.271 --> 17:46.440
Dobby is free.

17:52.071 --> 17:53.280
Oh, my gosh!

17:53.989 --> 17:57.034
- I was here the whole time though.
- What are you doing there?

17:57.785 --> 17:58.619
I'm hungry.

17:58.702 --> 18:01.663
There's a lot of food here,
but there's nothing to eat.

18:02.498 --> 18:03.999
You didn't leave?

18:04.792 --> 18:06.877
- Nobody told me to leave.
- Everyone left.

18:06.960 --> 18:08.295
My alcohol's still here.

18:08.378 --> 18:10.923
- I mean, aren't you looking for Yeon-su?
- What about you?

18:12.382 --> 18:14.885
But why are you talking so casually to me?

18:15.552 --> 18:19.556
I personally believe that people should be
respected according to their age.

18:19.640 --> 18:20.849
And I'm older than you.

18:21.767 --> 18:23.936
But do you really not know where Ung is?

18:24.019 --> 18:25.687
Of course I do.

18:25.771 --> 18:28.315
It's obvious where he'd be.

18:28.398 --> 18:30.400
He doesn't have any friends or hobbies.

18:30.484 --> 18:31.944
It's the same for Yeon-su.

18:32.027 --> 18:34.113
Is that why they dated?

18:35.114 --> 18:37.324
But he does have something like a hobby.

18:37.407 --> 18:39.034
It's obvious.

18:39.118 --> 18:40.661
They must be together right now.

18:42.287 --> 18:44.873
Isn't this your first time at this house?

18:44.957 --> 18:47.668
You've made yourself at home here.

18:47.751 --> 18:49.837
I even closed the bar today

18:49.920 --> 18:51.713
and came to have fun.

18:52.297 --> 18:53.882
I can't just sit around.

18:56.468 --> 18:58.929
How about a party to celebrate Choi Ung
without Ung?

19:04.351 --> 19:05.269
Sol-i.

19:06.061 --> 19:07.271
You're a genius.

19:22.578 --> 19:24.872
It feels like I've come back

19:24.955 --> 19:27.583
only three hours after I've run away.

19:28.458 --> 19:31.420
I ended up in front of Ung again.

19:34.131 --> 19:37.384
Okay, that's the worst thing
I've said this year.

19:42.306 --> 19:43.473
Hey…

19:44.224 --> 19:45.434
What are you doing here?

19:48.270 --> 19:49.354
Right.

19:50.480 --> 19:51.732
I thought…

19:53.942 --> 19:56.153
you were having a celebration party today.

19:56.236 --> 19:57.487
What about you?

19:57.571 --> 20:00.490
I just wanted to get some rest.

20:11.585 --> 20:13.378
You know this is really awkward, right?

20:13.462 --> 20:15.839
Really? I feel fine though.

20:16.673 --> 20:19.009
- Really?
- Yes. I'm totally fine.

20:19.635 --> 20:21.511
Why would we be awkward?

20:22.012 --> 20:25.307
I see. You must have decided
to pretend not to remember anything.

20:25.807 --> 20:28.185
- I don't know what you're saying.
- Kook Yeon-su.

20:31.313 --> 20:33.273
All right, fine. It's awkward.

20:33.357 --> 20:35.192
I got drunk and cried in front of my ex.

20:35.275 --> 20:37.152
So I feel really embarrassed. Happy?

20:43.700 --> 20:47.746
Like I said, running away
is a reasonable decision for me.

20:50.916 --> 20:52.167
But, at times,

20:53.335 --> 20:55.212
the choice hasn't always been mine.

20:57.464 --> 20:59.007
Let's go eat.

21:16.775 --> 21:19.069
EXCESSIVE LIFE
BEGINNING A JOURNEY

21:25.534 --> 21:29.913
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

21:33.959 --> 21:34.793
Here.

21:38.046 --> 21:39.756
I don't know what you're thinking.

21:39.840 --> 21:42.467
If you don't want to do this,
you can say no.

21:42.551 --> 21:43.593
It's volunteer work.

21:44.886 --> 21:46.722
You're not that warm-hearted, are you?

21:47.222 --> 21:49.099
This isn't helping you at all.

21:51.518 --> 21:54.146
NJ, drink this. I got it for you.

21:54.813 --> 21:56.148
Thank you.

21:56.231 --> 22:00.360
- You look much more pretty in person.
- Thanks.

22:05.991 --> 22:07.242
Don't you have any pride?

22:08.160 --> 22:12.039
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

22:12.122 --> 22:13.540
You all came here

22:13.623 --> 22:17.002
because NJ will drop the charges
if you did this, right?

22:17.085 --> 22:20.964
Yes. I heard everyone
who came last year was let off.

22:21.048 --> 22:22.382
Yes, she'll drop the charges.

22:22.466 --> 22:23.550
How do you know?

22:23.633 --> 22:27.220
Well, I actually came here last year too.

22:27.304 --> 22:28.805
- Oh, gosh.
- Gosh.

22:28.889 --> 22:30.682
Then you got caught again?

22:30.766 --> 22:32.726
I was just unlucky.

22:32.809 --> 22:35.979
Honestly, they say everything
is a malicious comment these days.

22:36.063 --> 22:39.983
Right. And to be honest, don't you
think this is kind of ridiculous?

22:40.650 --> 22:43.570
Volunteer work with people
who wrote bad comments about her?

22:43.653 --> 22:46.990
I don't know if she has
really high self-esteem or is smart.

22:47.074 --> 22:49.201
It's all for her image of course.

22:49.284 --> 22:50.619
She's a tough one.

22:51.286 --> 22:54.206
Anyway, just keep sucking up to her
and she'll let you off.

22:54.289 --> 22:56.833
Let's all hang in there
until this is over.

22:56.917 --> 22:59.753
Did you see those stickers of her face
on the lunch boxes?

23:00.420 --> 23:05.175
Nobody here wants to see
her face while eating.

23:05.258 --> 23:07.385
I tore it off already.

23:07.469 --> 23:10.514
She's so young, but she's as sly as a fox.

23:10.597 --> 23:12.933
But what kind of comment did you write?

23:13.016 --> 23:15.811
I didn't even make up stories about her.

23:16.394 --> 23:18.188
You know,

23:19.356 --> 23:22.901
there was a rumor
about NJ and her sponsors.

23:22.984 --> 23:24.820
And I just wrote about that a bit.

23:24.903 --> 23:27.864
NJ even had sponsors?

23:27.948 --> 23:29.783
I can't believe it! When?

23:30.534 --> 23:33.120
Her agency is going after
innocent citizens like us

23:33.203 --> 23:35.956
to keep it under wraps.

23:36.039 --> 23:37.290
I know, right?

23:37.374 --> 23:40.669
Remember when her first album
was a huge hit right after her debut?

23:40.752 --> 23:44.381
I heard her sponsors got her
all those commercials back then.

23:44.464 --> 23:47.592
That's how she bought
all those expensive buildings at her age.

23:47.676 --> 23:48.844
That's so crazy.

24:00.856 --> 24:02.399
Come on. What are you waiting for?

24:09.239 --> 24:10.657
WITH UNG

24:13.451 --> 24:15.579
Where have you been all day?

24:16.246 --> 24:17.205
Hello.

24:19.207 --> 24:20.458
Oh my, it's Yeon-su!

24:20.542 --> 24:21.918
Yeon-su's here?

24:22.002 --> 24:23.170
My goodness!

24:24.004 --> 24:25.005
Yeon-su!

24:25.589 --> 24:28.300
I'm so glad you're here.

24:28.884 --> 24:30.552
- You came to eat, right?
- Yes.

24:31.219 --> 24:32.304
Sit over there.

24:33.096 --> 24:35.265
Did you get home safe yesterday?

24:35.348 --> 24:37.392
Of course. Have a seat here.

24:37.475 --> 24:39.102
It's as if I'm not even here.

24:41.438 --> 24:43.148
- It's been such a long time.
- Yes.

24:43.231 --> 24:45.066
What do you want?
Tell me anything you want.

24:45.150 --> 24:48.945
Anything is fine.
Everything you make is so delicious.

24:49.029 --> 24:52.324
But still. Is there anything
you wanted to eat?

24:52.407 --> 24:56.620
Well, then, do you still make bean stew?

24:56.703 --> 24:59.998
Right! You used to love that!

25:00.540 --> 25:02.042
I'll make some right away.

25:02.125 --> 25:03.710
- Thank you.
- Mom, I want--

25:03.793 --> 25:06.630
I'll get you some meat and
other side dishes. Eat all you want, okay?

25:06.713 --> 25:08.465
- Thank you.
- Hey, I'm here.

25:09.132 --> 25:10.759
Weren't you here just a minute ago?

25:12.677 --> 25:14.804
What? When did Ung get here?

25:14.888 --> 25:16.056
Hang on.

25:17.265 --> 25:18.308
Ji-ung…

25:18.892 --> 25:22.270
Ji-ung asked me to call him if I saw Ung.

25:22.354 --> 25:24.314
All right. But don't call him.

25:24.397 --> 25:26.900
Ji-ung was looking for him everywhere.

25:26.983 --> 25:28.735
Just go, will you?

25:38.328 --> 25:40.413
Watching them again and again
won't get you anywhere.

25:40.497 --> 25:44.000
I'm sure I told you I don't want
the smell of food in here.

25:44.084 --> 25:46.086
I'm done eating.
Jeez, you're so sensitive.

25:47.420 --> 25:48.421
Did you eat?

25:49.256 --> 25:50.131
I did.

25:51.007 --> 25:52.884
Outside the editing room.

25:54.302 --> 25:56.680
Hey, I heard the cast ran away.

25:58.306 --> 26:02.060
I did think that they'd run away by now.

26:02.894 --> 26:05.981
- They haven't changed a single bit.
- You knew?

26:06.690 --> 26:10.318
They ran away after about two weeks
when we filmed ten years ago.

26:10.402 --> 26:11.403
Didn't you know?

26:12.320 --> 26:14.614
The day Yeon-su went home early
and Ung was absent?

26:14.698 --> 26:16.157
That's right.

26:16.241 --> 26:18.994
They both disappeared,
so we looked for them everywhere.

26:19.077 --> 26:21.705
- So where did you find them?
- We didn't.

26:22.289 --> 26:24.958
But they seemed to have
reached an agreement.

26:25.041 --> 26:27.377
They just returned as if nothing happened.

26:27.877 --> 26:29.462
- What?
- It's obvious.

26:29.546 --> 26:31.548
They'll return by themselves later,

26:31.631 --> 26:33.425
so just wait quietly.

26:33.508 --> 26:35.051
Don't worry.

26:35.969 --> 26:39.472
Chae-ran was looking for some lodging.
Are you going somewhere?

26:39.556 --> 26:40.765
Can I join you?

26:40.849 --> 26:43.101
This trip isn't for fun.

26:43.184 --> 26:46.021
Ms. Lee wanted to come too,
but don't even think about it.

26:46.104 --> 26:47.981
Grow up, the both of you.

26:53.945 --> 26:57.032
I made a list of places we can go to.

26:57.115 --> 27:00.410
- Should we decide after we find them?
- No, have things set in advance.

27:00.493 --> 27:02.329
Otherwise, we won't have enough time.

27:03.246 --> 27:06.249
I'll make sure to get them today,
no matter what.

27:10.462 --> 27:11.296
Is he useful?

27:11.379 --> 27:13.256
I told him to make a list of lodgings

27:13.340 --> 27:17.052
and he gave me about 20 pages of places
where newlyweds would go.

27:17.135 --> 27:19.637
He's really good at organizing stuff.

27:19.721 --> 27:21.723
I already feel nauseous.

27:21.806 --> 27:23.016
He's so different from me.

27:24.768 --> 27:26.186
Mr. Kim!

27:26.269 --> 27:28.271
Are you going out on business?
I can drive.

27:28.355 --> 27:29.647
No, it's fine.

27:30.690 --> 27:32.067
Hey, Intern. You can go--

27:32.150 --> 27:33.234
It's Im Tae-hun, sir.

27:33.818 --> 27:35.445
Okay, Intern. Why don't you--

27:35.528 --> 27:36.738
It's Im Tae-hun.

27:41.493 --> 27:43.411
All right.
I'll call you Imtern from now on.

27:43.495 --> 27:46.623
Imtern, go home and pack. Okay?

27:46.706 --> 27:48.041
Okay.

27:48.124 --> 27:49.918
- And Chae-ran, wrap up here and go home.
- Okay.

27:52.128 --> 27:53.797
- Imtern.
- Yes, sir.

28:14.901 --> 28:16.528
Are you uncomfortable here?

28:18.029 --> 28:20.573
No, I was thinking
of visiting soon anyway.

28:21.533 --> 28:25.078
I'm glad your parents seem healthy.

28:26.371 --> 28:29.541
They have aged quite a lot though.

28:31.000 --> 28:33.169
How about your grandma? Is she doing okay?

28:33.837 --> 28:35.755
Yes, she's good.

28:36.756 --> 28:37.924
I see.

28:46.391 --> 28:48.059
The radishes are really…

28:48.143 --> 28:49.936
You didn't answer me yet.

28:58.153 --> 28:59.863
How have you been?

29:02.157 --> 29:05.452
Well, I just graduated
and started working.

29:06.619 --> 29:07.537
Nothing much.

29:08.455 --> 29:09.414
I've been okay.

29:11.791 --> 29:12.792
Is that it?

29:13.626 --> 29:16.004
Yes. Nothing special.

29:17.756 --> 29:19.883
- Then yesterday--
- Yesterday,

29:19.966 --> 29:21.801
I was really drunk.

29:22.552 --> 29:24.929
It's embarrassing,
so just forget what happened.

29:25.013 --> 29:29.934
You know how stressed I was
working on this project.

29:37.984 --> 29:38.902
I enjoyed the food.

29:40.487 --> 29:41.654
I should get going.

29:44.532 --> 29:47.202
- Yeon-su, are you leaving already?
- My gosh.

29:47.285 --> 29:49.662
I really enjoyed the food.

29:49.746 --> 29:52.916
I didn't expect to come here,
so I didn't bring anything.

29:52.999 --> 29:54.834
Gosh, there's no need.

29:54.918 --> 29:58.046
You can visit us any time, all right?

29:58.129 --> 29:59.047
Okay.

29:59.130 --> 30:00.715
Oh, wait. Hang on.

30:00.799 --> 30:02.592
I packed some side dishes.

30:02.675 --> 30:04.093
No, it's fine.

30:04.177 --> 30:06.262
Have these with your grandmother.

30:07.138 --> 30:09.682
And bring her along next time.

30:10.350 --> 30:11.976
You didn't have to.

30:13.019 --> 30:15.522
But I'll enjoy these. Thank you.

30:15.605 --> 30:16.731
Come back next time.

30:16.815 --> 30:18.107
Take her home, Ung.

30:18.191 --> 30:19.692
I can go by myself.

30:19.776 --> 30:21.486
Of course not!

30:21.569 --> 30:22.821
Jeez.

30:22.904 --> 30:24.197
Come back next time, okay?

30:24.280 --> 30:26.616
I'll see you next time. Bye.

30:26.699 --> 30:27.992
Get home safe.

30:29.953 --> 30:31.204
See you next time.

30:38.211 --> 30:39.838
How do they seem to you?

30:40.839 --> 30:42.882
I have no clue.

30:51.891 --> 30:53.268
I've always said this,

30:53.351 --> 30:56.771
but you should be good to your parents.
They're so kind and nice.

30:59.816 --> 31:01.067
Are you going home?

31:01.651 --> 31:04.779
Ji-ung won't still
be waiting there, would he?

31:05.989 --> 31:08.700
We both went AWOL without telling them,

31:08.783 --> 31:11.494
so let's apologize tomorrow
and start filming again…

31:11.578 --> 31:13.830
Right. This is how I felt.

31:15.623 --> 31:17.959
This is how I felt while dating you.

31:19.419 --> 31:21.337
I was just waiting like an idiot,

31:22.213 --> 31:25.258
watching you walk away, step by step.

31:25.341 --> 31:26.467
It was always like that.

31:28.261 --> 31:30.305
What do you mean?

31:30.889 --> 31:33.850
When you said you were okay,
I had to just accept it.

31:34.893 --> 31:36.436
When you said nothing was wrong,

31:37.228 --> 31:39.063
I had to say I worried for no reason.

31:40.315 --> 31:41.941
And when you wanted to break up,

31:42.775 --> 31:45.528
I had to accept it
without knowing the reason.

31:46.613 --> 31:48.573
And when I met you again,

31:49.866 --> 31:51.784
I didn't know how you'd been

31:53.828 --> 31:56.414
or what you were thinking…

31:59.417 --> 32:02.712
but I had to just accept things
without knowing anything.

32:02.795 --> 32:05.089
"Attack is the secret of defense."

32:06.257 --> 32:08.509
It really feels like you're back, Yeon-su.

32:10.803 --> 32:12.055
Choi Ung.

32:12.138 --> 32:14.265
I'm really sick of this.

32:16.476 --> 32:18.519
I guess that's what I'm doing right now.

32:21.898 --> 32:25.234
But this wasn't my choice.

32:47.173 --> 32:48.591
One, two, three!

32:50.426 --> 32:51.594
- Good job.
- Good job.

32:51.678 --> 32:53.846
- Good job.
- Good job.

32:53.930 --> 32:55.848
- Good job.
- Thank you.

32:55.932 --> 32:57.350
- Good job.
- NJ.

32:58.393 --> 33:01.646
I had a really meaningful experience today
thanks to you.

33:01.729 --> 33:02.855
Thank you.

33:04.023 --> 33:08.277
We were able to
reflect on ourselves today thanks to you.

33:08.361 --> 33:11.239
Thank you for giving us this opportunity.

33:11.322 --> 33:14.784
- So you're going to let us off, right?
- Jeez.

33:15.618 --> 33:18.246
We'll do our best
to make up for our mistakes.

33:18.913 --> 33:22.959
And we'll tell everyone
about how cool you were today.

33:23.042 --> 33:24.085
Okay?

33:26.921 --> 33:29.132
All right.

33:32.385 --> 33:34.220
- Director.
- Yes?

33:34.303 --> 33:37.265
I'm sorry, but I can't come anymore.

33:37.348 --> 33:39.892
- Why?
- I thought they'd stop eventually.

33:39.976 --> 33:42.812
I didn't know people would
keep leaving malicious comments.

33:44.605 --> 33:45.773
They're not my fans.

33:46.941 --> 33:48.943
They're just malicious commenters I sued.

33:49.027 --> 33:50.611
- Hey, NJ.
- What?

33:50.695 --> 33:52.280
Who? Me?

33:52.989 --> 33:56.034
You always seemed to call me bitch.

33:59.537 --> 34:02.165
- I'm not dropping the charges.
- What?

34:02.248 --> 34:03.583
Good work today.

34:04.459 --> 34:08.463
Thank you for joining me when I asked
if you wanted to do volunteer work.

34:08.546 --> 34:10.131
Goodbye then.

34:10.214 --> 34:13.259
- But please…
- You can't do this!

34:14.010 --> 34:16.012
You've conned us.

34:16.095 --> 34:19.849
You said you'd drop the charges.
This is ridiculous.

34:22.518 --> 34:26.397
I don't think I ever promised
to drop the charges.

34:27.815 --> 34:29.942
You ate with me here last year, right?

34:30.026 --> 34:32.361
Did you do it again because you missed me?

34:32.445 --> 34:33.780
Well, that was…

34:34.822 --> 34:38.034
It was constructive criticism.
Do you think everyone is out to get you?

34:40.912 --> 34:44.624
Should I read the comments
you wrote about me then?

34:45.458 --> 34:48.002
Let's see how constructive it is.

34:48.086 --> 34:52.882
Hey, you're just abusing your power
against innocent citizens.

34:52.965 --> 34:54.425
We're all busy people, you know.

34:54.509 --> 34:56.636
You were just making us waste our time!

34:57.720 --> 35:00.890
You'd better suck up to me
if you at least want a lower sentence.

35:01.599 --> 35:02.725
Are you sure about this?

35:05.478 --> 35:07.897
- Jeez.
- Excuse me.

35:08.689 --> 35:09.690
NJ.

35:10.191 --> 35:14.112
As you know,
I only made this mistake once.

35:14.695 --> 35:17.615
If I get indicted,
I'll have a hard time getting a job.

35:18.533 --> 35:22.203
Can you please let me off this time?
My life is at stake here.

35:25.665 --> 35:28.835
All right. You only did it once.

35:30.211 --> 35:31.754
So I'll sue you just once.

35:32.547 --> 35:34.715
If you do it twice,
I'll sue you twice too.

35:35.758 --> 35:40.263
Come on. People make mistakes.

35:40.346 --> 35:41.848
Do you have to be so cruel?

35:41.931 --> 35:45.434
What kind of a mistake led
you to sexually harass me online?

35:45.518 --> 35:47.103
Your ID is Bibibik, right?

35:47.895 --> 35:49.856
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

35:50.898 --> 35:53.359
There were articles
about how this was a place

35:53.442 --> 35:55.153
for reconciliation and forgiveness.

35:55.236 --> 35:57.196
Go and tell people it isn't.

35:57.280 --> 36:01.742
Tell everyone that I was a crazy bitch
who was bent on suing you.

36:01.826 --> 36:04.120
And that I was acting unlike myself.

36:06.205 --> 36:07.415
Go and tell people this

36:08.749 --> 36:10.042
as you've always done.

36:11.085 --> 36:12.879
- Wait, NJ!
- Drop the charges!

36:12.962 --> 36:14.380
That's enough.

36:15.006 --> 36:16.507
Do you even have a conscience?

36:23.222 --> 36:24.765
Darn it.

36:25.975 --> 36:27.518
What did I say now?

36:27.602 --> 36:31.063
I just want to go home and rest.

36:37.653 --> 36:39.030
WHY DID YOU TWO SUDDENLY GO AWOL?

36:41.657 --> 36:43.826
- Choi Ung!
- Choi Ung!

36:43.910 --> 36:45.786
Congratulations!

36:45.870 --> 36:48.331
You're far away right now,

36:48.414 --> 36:49.999
but we're congratulating you.

36:50.082 --> 36:51.667
Congratulations!

36:51.751 --> 36:54.086
Ung here says that he's really happy.

36:54.170 --> 36:57.340
Right, Ung? You're happy, aren't you?
Why don't you smile?

36:57.423 --> 37:00.635
Hey, I heard you're earning a fortune.

37:00.718 --> 37:03.137
Can't you buy my bar? Please?

37:03.221 --> 37:07.099
Ung, this is our success story!

37:07.183 --> 37:10.061
I can't believe the dim-witted Ung

37:10.144 --> 37:12.521
has succeeded this much.

37:12.605 --> 37:14.190
I can't…

37:14.941 --> 37:18.277
I can't believe

37:18.361 --> 37:22.031
I saw my idiot Ung succeed…

37:22.114 --> 37:25.201
Why are you crying?
You're making me cry too.

37:25.284 --> 37:27.662
He didn't even get to eat properly…

37:27.745 --> 37:29.288
Don't cry. You'll sober up.

37:29.372 --> 37:31.666
He suffered so much…

37:32.416 --> 37:33.417
Ung!

37:33.918 --> 37:37.672
You have to be happy, all right?

37:39.715 --> 37:43.177
It looks more like
they're holding my funeral.

37:44.804 --> 37:46.180
Should I report them?

37:46.973 --> 37:48.724
Eun-ho, that jerk.

37:49.433 --> 37:50.559
What?

37:50.643 --> 37:52.270
NJ

37:59.485 --> 38:00.778
This is how I felt.

38:01.570 --> 38:03.698
I was just waiting like an idiot,

38:03.781 --> 38:05.825
watching you walk away, step by step.

38:06.409 --> 38:08.327
It was always like that.

38:09.287 --> 38:10.913
I'm really sick of this.

38:10.997 --> 38:12.456
Is that you, Yeon-su?

38:17.336 --> 38:19.839
Why are you standing there like that?

38:19.922 --> 38:22.133
- Did you just arrive?
- Yes.

38:23.301 --> 38:25.094
What's that in your hand?

38:30.725 --> 38:32.977
Grandma, I'll be back in a moment.

38:33.060 --> 38:34.979
Didn't you just get home?

38:37.940 --> 38:40.109
Good job.
You should have done that earlier.

38:40.192 --> 38:41.986
It's not something
you can forgive that easily.

38:42.069 --> 38:44.572
"The kindhearted NJ
who forgives everyone"?

38:44.655 --> 38:45.990
That's nonsense.

38:46.073 --> 38:47.366
We'll tell the boss

38:47.450 --> 38:50.036
that you won't be dropping charges
for anyone anymore.

38:50.745 --> 38:51.871
Those jerks.

38:53.372 --> 38:54.457
But…

38:55.333 --> 38:57.960
why did you want to
meet them in person every time?

38:59.337 --> 39:00.504
I just thought

39:02.048 --> 39:04.925
that it'd be less scary
if I saw the people behind it.

39:06.427 --> 39:08.763
Just avoid them. Run away.

39:09.930 --> 39:11.182
It's okay to do that.

39:19.357 --> 39:21.484
That's why I'm running away today.

39:23.402 --> 39:24.779
To that person?

39:29.950 --> 39:30.868
Yes.

39:33.537 --> 39:34.830
Mr. Choi!

39:35.998 --> 39:37.166
My gosh.

39:37.666 --> 39:39.168
Darn it.

39:40.211 --> 39:41.170
Hey…

39:43.881 --> 39:46.133
I guess I called at the perfect timing.

39:46.801 --> 39:49.970
Were you wandering around
after running away from home?

39:50.054 --> 39:52.098
Running away from home at this age?

39:52.181 --> 39:53.349
I was just

39:54.058 --> 39:56.519
trying to have some time to myself.

39:56.602 --> 39:59.105
If you don't want
to do the documentary, just don't.

39:59.188 --> 40:03.067
It'd be quite overwhelming for someone
who isn't a celebrity.

40:13.369 --> 40:14.912
It's okay. Come here.

40:15.413 --> 40:16.956
Bring your bags.

40:23.671 --> 40:26.841
I can't believe this! Are you really NJ?

40:26.924 --> 40:29.051
You're really NJ?

40:29.135 --> 40:31.095
Yes. Do you have a pen?

40:39.353 --> 40:43.566
Hey, kid. You should ask for permission
before taking photos of someone.

40:43.649 --> 40:44.900
Can I take a photo?

40:44.984 --> 40:46.360
No, you can't.

40:46.444 --> 40:49.155
There are lots of pretty photos online,
so look at those.

40:49.738 --> 40:50.614
Here.

40:51.657 --> 40:53.784
Do you know what scarcity is?

40:54.577 --> 40:55.619
You know rare items, right?

40:55.703 --> 40:57.121
- Yes.
- Yes.

40:57.830 --> 41:00.332
If you want
your bags to become rare items,

41:00.416 --> 41:04.378
you shouldn't tell anyone
that I'm here. Got that?

41:05.045 --> 41:06.255
- Yes.
- Yes.

41:06.338 --> 41:08.132
If you tell people I'm here,

41:08.716 --> 41:11.135
I'll sign everyone's bags.

41:11.844 --> 41:13.721
- So you shouldn't, right?
- Right.

41:13.804 --> 41:15.848
Run along now.
I was talking with my friend.

41:16.432 --> 41:17.850
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

41:23.105 --> 41:25.649
Even little kids recognize you.

41:26.233 --> 41:27.651
It must be tiring.

41:28.569 --> 41:31.238
Ordinary people like you
won't ever know what it's like.

41:32.448 --> 41:35.826
Wait. I think you'd understand a bit now.

41:37.161 --> 41:40.122
Well, there were people who recognized me

41:40.206 --> 41:42.625
because of that stupid documentary.

41:42.708 --> 41:44.627
Then why are you filming it again?

41:45.419 --> 41:47.254
It just happened.

41:47.755 --> 41:50.674
I've fallen into my own trap, I guess.

41:50.758 --> 41:53.344
That happens sometimes.

42:04.230 --> 42:06.023
Did you just laugh at me?

42:06.941 --> 42:08.692
Let's have lunch together.

42:09.235 --> 42:11.987
Well, I just ate.

42:15.282 --> 42:20.037
Mr. Choi. I really didn't want
to say this myself,

42:20.579 --> 42:24.959
but I'm introverted and sensitive
even though I might not seem so.

42:25.042 --> 42:27.336
My blood type is A and my MBTI is ISFP.

42:28.003 --> 42:30.714
So I wrote some things in my heart diary.

42:31.632 --> 42:32.925
What diary?

42:33.008 --> 42:33.884
First.

42:34.510 --> 42:36.971
"Mr. Choi got famous
because I bought one of his works,

42:37.054 --> 42:39.598
but why doesn't he want to buy me a meal?"

42:39.682 --> 42:40.724
Second.

42:40.808 --> 42:45.145
"I commissioned him to draw my building,
but why doesn't he even contact me?"

42:45.896 --> 42:47.356
And third.

42:47.439 --> 42:49.733
"I made him even more popular

42:49.817 --> 42:52.486
by going to his drawing show
when I wasn't even invited,

42:52.570 --> 42:55.281
but why won't he still buy me a meal?"

42:55.906 --> 42:59.243
- Well, I--
- Those are the three debts you have.

42:59.326 --> 43:00.869
How will you repay me?

43:13.465 --> 43:16.719
Does he think he's the only one
who can get upset?

43:17.303 --> 43:19.680
When did he ever tell me anything?

43:19.763 --> 43:21.682
Choi Ung was always the one…

43:23.017 --> 43:25.185
Why isn't he picking up?

43:25.269 --> 43:26.812
…who hid when he got upset.

43:32.901 --> 43:36.113
But this…

43:38.282 --> 43:41.744
I didn't expect
something like this to happen.

43:43.162 --> 43:44.288
Excuse me.

43:47.958 --> 43:48.959
Hey…

43:52.338 --> 43:56.216
Why are you so clumsy?

43:57.718 --> 44:00.971
Anyway, I thought everyone
would pretend not to have eaten

44:01.055 --> 44:02.723
if I asked to have a meal together.

44:03.223 --> 44:04.933
You're so difficult.

44:06.769 --> 44:08.937
NJ…

44:09.021 --> 44:12.650
You keep contacting me

44:13.359 --> 44:15.319
and finding me…

44:17.112 --> 44:20.074
I've been pretty clueless, haven't I?

44:22.326 --> 44:25.204
Weren't you pretending to be clueless?

44:25.287 --> 44:26.747
I guess it's true…

44:28.999 --> 44:31.377
I'm sorry.
I should have brought it up first.

44:31.460 --> 44:33.128
I know, right?

44:33.712 --> 44:36.048
It's embarrassing
to have to say it myself.

44:38.008 --> 44:39.093
Well…

44:42.638 --> 44:45.349
Since you bought three drawings,
I'll give you one for free.

44:45.432 --> 44:48.060
I don't usually do this,
but since you're NJ,

44:48.143 --> 44:50.145
- if there's anything--
- Mr. Choi.

44:50.854 --> 44:52.398
I have a lot of money.

44:52.481 --> 44:55.734
Do you think I'm doing this
just to get a free drawing?

44:56.360 --> 44:59.113
What? Then why are you
being so nice to me?

45:00.739 --> 45:02.408
So I don't have a reason.

45:02.950 --> 45:04.868
No, that's not what I meant.

45:04.952 --> 45:07.371
- Why would someone like you--
- Because I like you.

45:07.454 --> 45:08.330
What?

45:09.206 --> 45:10.999
- Oh my!
- My gosh!

45:11.083 --> 45:14.169
Why do you keep dropping your ice cream?

45:15.087 --> 45:16.296
What do you mean?

45:18.173 --> 45:20.759
I had a really tough day today.

45:21.385 --> 45:25.139
I don't want to whine about it
because it's normal for me.

45:26.473 --> 45:27.808
But…

45:28.392 --> 45:30.686
I feel better when I see you.

45:31.687 --> 45:34.064
At first, I felt better
when I saw your drawings.

45:34.815 --> 45:36.775
But now, I feel it with you too.

45:37.943 --> 45:41.071
That's my reason for seeing you.

45:42.072 --> 45:44.366
So stop getting so startled
whenever you see me.

45:45.159 --> 45:46.702
And don't look so shocked.

45:47.619 --> 45:49.037
I'm not saying I love you,

45:49.121 --> 45:50.998
and I'm not asking you out.

45:51.081 --> 45:52.708
I'm just saying that I like you.

45:54.168 --> 45:57.796
Maybe it's just because
you look like Tofu.

45:59.465 --> 46:00.716
"Tofu"?

46:00.799 --> 46:02.384
Yes. My dog.

46:03.677 --> 46:04.845
I see, your dog.

46:09.099 --> 46:10.893
Are you going somewhere?

46:10.976 --> 46:13.687
Some kids just don't listen.

46:14.563 --> 46:16.648
I should get going. Let's hang out again.

46:17.524 --> 46:19.359
You should go home too.

46:20.402 --> 46:21.612
Let's go!

46:23.113 --> 46:24.907
- Go!
- It's NJ!

46:24.990 --> 46:26.283
Is it really NJ?

46:26.366 --> 46:28.702
- They're back again.
- NJ! I want your autograph too!

46:28.785 --> 46:30.704
- NJ!
- There she is!

46:37.544 --> 46:39.379
You're unbelievable.

46:39.463 --> 46:40.964
Were you looking for me all day?

46:41.048 --> 46:43.550
No, I just started looking for you.

46:43.634 --> 46:45.719
I found you earlier than expected.

46:45.802 --> 46:47.429
You didn't even go that far.

46:48.263 --> 46:50.724
- What were you doing?
- Just taking a walk.

46:59.650 --> 47:00.651
Really?

47:01.193 --> 47:02.903
Then why did you run away today?

47:03.904 --> 47:05.155
I needed a break.

47:05.239 --> 47:07.032
You needed a break?

47:07.115 --> 47:10.911
Yes. I wanted to experience some freedom.

47:10.994 --> 47:14.081
Is that so? You should have told me.
You'll get to soon.

47:14.164 --> 47:16.250
- What?
- Never mind.

47:17.376 --> 47:19.002
Are you going to keep shooting?

47:21.463 --> 47:24.007
- I'm just confirming. Don't answer that.
- Hey.

47:28.637 --> 47:30.222
Did you fight with Ung again?

47:30.305 --> 47:34.142
We didn't really fight.
He just got angry at me.

47:34.226 --> 47:36.562
When did he become so short-tempered?

47:37.271 --> 47:38.480
When do you think?

47:42.818 --> 47:44.403
Fine. Everything's my fault.

47:44.945 --> 47:47.990
Not everything. Maybe about half.

47:48.073 --> 47:49.992
Half and half with Ung.

47:50.075 --> 47:51.159
Half and half?

47:51.702 --> 47:54.746
Breaking up
isn't usually just one person's fault.

47:54.830 --> 47:56.415
It's the same for both sides.

48:02.045 --> 48:03.297
What is it?

48:04.256 --> 48:06.592
You seem to know a lot about dating.

48:07.426 --> 48:08.468
What?

48:08.552 --> 48:10.596
So, are you seeing someone?

48:12.347 --> 48:13.432
My gosh.

48:14.933 --> 48:17.394
You're not. Have you ever dated before?

48:17.477 --> 48:20.063
Yeon-su. There are two kinds of men
in this world.

48:20.147 --> 48:22.899
Men who can't date,
and men who don't date.

48:22.983 --> 48:24.568
You're someone who can't.

48:27.154 --> 48:28.363
You're so ridiculous.

48:28.447 --> 48:31.867
You'd be shocked to find out
what kind of person I am.

48:31.950 --> 48:33.619
Really? What kind of person are you?

48:34.995 --> 48:36.955
I'm a bit of a bad boy.

48:38.498 --> 48:40.208
You know what a homme fatale is, right?

48:40.292 --> 48:43.587
It means I could be fatal to women.

48:43.670 --> 48:47.007
I try to keep my attractiveness hidden
so I won't harm others.

48:47.090 --> 48:51.637
Kim Ji-ung.
When did you become so shameless?

48:52.763 --> 48:53.805
You're so funny.

48:55.015 --> 48:57.100
That wasn't a joke. I'm serious.

48:57.184 --> 49:01.104
I guess you were a bit popular
when we were in high school.

49:01.188 --> 49:02.564
You finally get me.

49:02.648 --> 49:03.649
Why, though?

49:04.232 --> 49:06.109
Hey, that's kind of mean.

49:06.193 --> 49:08.695
I guess it helped that
you were the student president.

49:09.780 --> 49:11.865
You just didn't know me much back then.

49:16.620 --> 49:18.246
I'm so drunk right now.

49:20.957 --> 49:21.917
That idiot…

49:23.168 --> 49:24.461
Is that Sol-i?

49:25.462 --> 49:27.798
What a way to end a terrible day.

49:28.632 --> 49:29.800
Sol-i!

49:29.883 --> 49:30.884
Sol-i.

49:31.426 --> 49:32.511
Sol-i!

49:33.428 --> 49:34.930
Yeon-su!

49:38.934 --> 49:40.102
What is this?

49:40.185 --> 49:42.020
- I'm drunk.
- My gosh.

49:52.948 --> 49:54.157
Eun-ho?

50:04.251 --> 50:06.211
Have you finally croaked?

50:19.516 --> 50:20.642
Maybe…

50:21.518 --> 50:23.645
rather than a raise,
you're better off gone.

50:26.064 --> 50:27.858
You made a total mess in here.

50:30.819 --> 50:32.070
I think I'm going to puke.

50:33.447 --> 50:35.866
- You're unbelievable.
- I'm going to puke.

50:37.659 --> 50:39.327
You're such a pain.

50:41.288 --> 50:43.039
Is it okay for her to sleep here?

50:43.123 --> 50:44.291
Her dad's a minister.

50:44.374 --> 50:46.710
Believe it or not,
her family's very religious.

50:46.793 --> 50:48.378
They don't know she drinks.

50:48.462 --> 50:49.838
I love you, God.

50:50.672 --> 50:53.008
How can they not know
when she's running a bar?

50:53.091 --> 50:54.926
You should see her act.

50:55.010 --> 50:57.387
She should have been an actress,
not a writer.

50:58.305 --> 51:00.682
- I love you.
- Just go to sleep.

51:01.183 --> 51:03.560
I'm sorry you got dragged into this mess.

51:04.060 --> 51:07.063
- What's going on here?
- Grandma!

51:07.147 --> 51:10.859
Oh, my. Aren't you Ji-ung?

51:10.942 --> 51:12.319
It's so nice to see you.

51:12.402 --> 51:15.197
How have you been?
It looks like you got younger.

51:15.280 --> 51:16.490
Come on.

51:17.199 --> 51:19.868
Since when were you two so close?

51:19.951 --> 51:23.497
Ji-ung's the sweetest boy I've ever seen.

51:24.581 --> 51:25.707
Have you eaten?

51:25.791 --> 51:27.751
- Why don't I give you something to eat?
- All right.

51:28.502 --> 51:29.711
But what's this stench?

51:31.213 --> 51:33.173
It's me, it's me

51:33.256 --> 51:35.675
That little brat! Is she drunk again?

51:35.759 --> 51:38.136
- Can you leave my room now?
- That wench.

51:38.220 --> 51:40.555
What do we do with her?

51:43.767 --> 51:45.393
Welcome!

51:59.241 --> 52:02.285
Ung! My Ung who ran away.

52:02.786 --> 52:05.288
I knew you'd become successful.

52:05.997 --> 52:08.416
I'm so proud of you.

52:09.543 --> 52:11.044
I'm still not forgiving you.

52:12.629 --> 52:14.089
Continued on the back.

52:15.465 --> 52:18.468
You may be a loser who failed at love,

52:19.052 --> 52:20.720
but you succeeded in your career.

52:20.804 --> 52:22.472
Let's work hard!

52:23.598 --> 52:25.433
It's me, Sol-i.

52:25.517 --> 52:27.853
Can you lend me 20 million won?

52:29.604 --> 52:30.647
You jerk!

52:47.205 --> 52:49.958
So what are you doing these days?

52:51.835 --> 52:53.336
- I'm filming Ung.
- The documentary?

52:53.420 --> 52:55.839
Will it be on TV, then?

52:55.922 --> 52:57.591
Yes, of course.

53:16.151 --> 53:17.694
What are you doing here so early?

53:17.777 --> 53:19.279
Get in. Let's go for a drive.

53:20.030 --> 53:21.239
Are you half-asleep?

53:21.323 --> 53:23.366
You said you wanted to experience freedom.

53:24.159 --> 53:27.370
- Let's get some fresh air.
- No, I can't be bothered.

53:29.831 --> 53:31.249
Hey!

53:31.333 --> 53:34.586
What are you doing?
You'll wake the whole neighborhood.

53:35.170 --> 53:37.631
- Why don't I?
- Hey, Ji-ung!

53:37.714 --> 53:38.882
Get in.

53:44.638 --> 53:46.431
In American horror films,

53:46.514 --> 53:50.101
crime usually happens
suddenly in broad daylight.

53:54.731 --> 53:55.774
What are you doing?

54:02.948 --> 54:04.324
Where are you going?

54:08.745 --> 54:09.996
What?

54:15.543 --> 54:19.798
They strike when you have your guard down.

54:34.312 --> 54:36.231
And the criminal usually ends up

54:37.774 --> 54:39.025
being an acquaintance.

54:44.155 --> 54:45.407
What…

54:46.032 --> 54:47.367
What are you doing?

55:21.985 --> 55:24.154
Choi Ung's surprise show!

55:24.237 --> 55:26.031
How many fans will be here today?

55:26.614 --> 55:28.199
All right. Get out.

55:28.283 --> 55:30.910
- Take off your blindfold!
- Hey!

55:31.494 --> 55:33.329
What do you think you're doing?

55:33.413 --> 55:36.583
How could you not tell me anything
during the whole trip?

55:36.666 --> 55:37.667
What…

55:38.376 --> 55:39.794
Where's your boss?

55:39.878 --> 55:41.171
I'm going to sue…

55:48.678 --> 55:49.971
Hey, Ji-ung!

55:52.098 --> 55:53.391
You're here.

55:53.475 --> 55:56.770
Ji-ung. This isn't funny at all.

55:56.853 --> 56:00.148
I don't know what you're up to, but…

56:06.029 --> 56:09.532
So the genre here isn't romance…

56:11.534 --> 56:14.788
We're all here now.
We're staying here for three days.

56:15.997 --> 56:18.917
- We have seven fans today!
- …it's horror.

56:19.000 --> 56:20.210
Round of applause!

56:21.294 --> 56:24.130
You might have noticed,
but you can't leave without a car.

56:24.798 --> 56:27.258
If you want to leave,
you'll have to start walking now.

56:27.967 --> 56:29.302
It'll take days though.

56:29.385 --> 56:30.845
Ji-ung!

56:34.974 --> 56:37.060
A cliche horror-thriller film

56:37.727 --> 56:39.062
that's always released

56:39.646 --> 56:41.272
around this time of the year.

56:47.695 --> 56:49.447
EPILOGUE

56:49.531 --> 56:50.657
- Sir.
- Yes.

56:50.740 --> 56:52.033
Choi Ung isn't here today.

56:53.493 --> 56:54.911
What? He's not here?

56:54.994 --> 56:55.995
No.

56:57.539 --> 57:00.750
No wonder. He wasn't picking up earlier.

57:10.009 --> 57:11.261
Sir.

57:12.178 --> 57:13.179
Yes?

57:14.097 --> 57:16.683
Can I leave school early?

57:16.766 --> 57:18.226
Why? Are you not well?

57:20.061 --> 57:20.979
No.

57:21.062 --> 57:23.857
Right. You must have been
overworked these days.

57:23.940 --> 57:25.400
Go and get some rest.

57:32.031 --> 57:33.283
NO LONGER HUMAN
CHEKHOV SHORT STORIES

57:48.465 --> 57:49.966
What are you doing here?

57:50.633 --> 57:51.676
Getting a book.

57:52.343 --> 57:54.137
You skipped school to come here?

57:55.054 --> 57:56.306
No one would know I'm here.

57:57.432 --> 57:58.766
What about you?

58:00.602 --> 58:01.644
I got off school early.

58:06.149 --> 58:07.775
Are you going to read that?

58:09.402 --> 58:10.236
Yes.

58:11.905 --> 58:16.034
Well, it might be a bit difficult for you.
Are you sure you can?

58:16.117 --> 58:20.246
It won't be easy to understand
Nietzsche's philosophical ideology.

58:21.581 --> 58:22.832
THUS SPOKE ZARATHUSTRA

58:24.292 --> 58:27.670
So just give it to me.
It'll be better if I read it.

58:28.546 --> 58:29.839
Eternal return.

58:29.923 --> 58:33.051
It's the concept that the universe
is recurring infinitely.

58:34.385 --> 58:37.096
And in its eternal recurrence,

58:37.180 --> 58:39.724
our existence also recurs infinitely
and continues to do so.

58:39.807 --> 58:43.144
I got curious about the eternity of time.

58:43.228 --> 58:44.437
So I'm reading it again.

58:49.651 --> 58:50.735
Okay.

58:51.402 --> 58:52.737
Return if when you're done.

58:53.988 --> 58:55.240
About yesterday…

58:56.157 --> 58:57.534
I guess

58:58.785 --> 59:01.246
I was a bit harsh.

59:05.542 --> 59:06.876
Is that why you ran away?

59:07.877 --> 59:09.879
Yes. I thought you'd be uncomfortable.

59:16.052 --> 59:18.638
I'm hungry. Let's go eat.

59:21.933 --> 59:28.940
CATCH ME IF YOU CAN

59:50.211 --> 59:52.338
Which trip was the most memorable?

59:52.422 --> 59:54.799
I think I love you.

59:54.882 --> 59:57.594
We really came on another trip.
And it's farther away.

59:57.677 --> 59:59.596
- I'm disappointed.
- NJ!

59:59.679 --> 01:00:01.472
It confuses me the more I film you two.

01:00:01.556 --> 01:00:04.559
whether it's because of
your past relationship…

01:00:04.642 --> 01:00:07.020
We're not going to break up.

01:00:07.103 --> 01:00:08.896
Just come to me like you did today.

01:00:09.564 --> 01:00:14.569
Subtitle translation by: Ju-young Park
